      "content": "I apologize for the confusion. Under GDPR, you must ensure that personal data, such as customer email addresses and shipping information, is processed lawfully, fairly, and transparently. You must obtain explicit consent from customers before collecting their data, and you must inform them about the purpose of data collection and how it will be used.\n\nYou are required to store personal data securely, using appropriate technical measures to prevent unauthorized access, accidental loss, or damage. Regularly review and update your security measures to address any potential risks.\n\nCustomers have the right to access their personal data, correct any inaccuracies, and request the deletion of their data. You must also report any data breaches to the relevant supervisory authority within 72 hours of becoming aware of the breach.\n\nIn summary, GDPR requires you to obtain explicit consent, inform customers about data usage, store data securely, allow customers to access and correct their data, and report data breaches. By adhering to these principles, you will be well-prepared for your upcoming audit.",
